{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"581f45644d92803ae8652802eb862b4a313c03ba3a4d2e7508d07c24e6dd4b6b","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-reading gates (review-plan)","key_entities":["review-plan","rebar.llm.gate_source.resolve_gate_handle","rebar.signing._gate_commit_sha()","rebar._build_info.COMMIT","hatch_build.py","verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets","verify.overlap_enabled"],"problem_keywords":["gate run","build drift","stale binary","version mismatch","code-reading gate","config unknown key"],"propositions":["A gate run does not detect when its running build binary is behind the base ref it pins, allowing stale code to review current material silently.","When the running build's commit is a strict ancestor of the pinned sha, a single advisory warning must be emitted naming the build sha, commit date, pinned sha, and drift count, without failing the run or altering the verdict.","Configuration unknown-key warnings must reflect whether drift was detected, using 'may predate' language when drift is confirmed instead of suggesting a typo.","The drift detection must be silent when provenance is unavailable, when the build sha is not present in the target repo, or when the build is at or ahead of the pinned sha."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787555104296403001,"uuid":"2ed0a6b6-2d47-4ae2-8b3f-fd8eb9bdfe55"}